 *
 * TR_INPUT_NPU builds only (CMakeLists.txt): the HP now owns I2C1 (0x49011000,
 * the camera SCCB bus, its own unstick sequence in hp_vision -- design sec 2).
 * The HE's display shield (e1m_evk_rk055hdmipi4ma0.overlay) ALSO enables
 * &i2c1 on the SAME pads (P3_7 I2C1_SCL_B / P7_2 I2C1_SDA_C -- the EVK's own
 * "display + camera control I2C" bus, shared by design, not a routing bug):
 * with TR_CAMERA/classical detect this HE-side i2c1 is how the panel's touch
 * controller would be reached; with TR_INPUT_NPU this game never touches
 * touch at all, and the HE enabling the SAME controller races the HP's own
 * pull-up setup and its camera transfers (reviewer finding, fix round 1) --
 * two DesignWare i2c_dw instances driving one physical bus from two cores is
 * a contention hazard regardless of whether either side is idle at any
 * given instant. Applied last (EXTRA_DTC_OVERLAY_FILE, after every shield)
 * so this status="disabled" wins over the shield's status="okay".
 */
&i2c1 {
	status = "disabled";
};
